==English==
[[File:Branched juniper twig with shots.jpg|thumb|A twig]]

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
{{etymon|en|id=stick|:inh|enm:twig|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|twig}}, {{m|enm|twyg}}, {{m|enm|twigge}}, {{m|enm|twygge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|twicg|twigg}}, {{m|ang|twicg}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*twiggu|t=small twig, shoot}}, apparently a diminutive of {{der|en|gmw-pro|*twig|t=branch, twig}} (whence also {{cog|ang|twiġ}} and {{m|ang|twiġa}}), from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*twīgą}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*dwigʰom}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*dwóh₁}}. More at [[two]].
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|twiich}}, {{m|frr|twiig|t=twig}}, {{cog|stq|Twiech|t=branch, twig}}, {{cog|fy|twiich|t=twig}}, {{cog|nl|twijg|t=twig}}, {{cog|de|Zweig|t=branch, twig; section}}, {{cog|nds-de|Twieg|t=branch, twig}}, {{cog|lb|Zwäig|t=twig}}, {{cog|yi|צווײַג|t=branch}}; also {{cog|cu|двигъ|t=branch}}, {{cog|sq|degë|t=branch}}.
{{col-bottom}}

