====Noun====
{{swp}}
{{en-noun}}

# A small thin [[branch]] of a [[tree]] or [[bush]].
#: {{ux|en|They used '''twigs''' and leaves as a base to start the fire.}}
#* {{RQ:Bindloss Dust of Conflict|chapter=1|passage=A beech wood with silver firs in it rolled down the face of the hill, and the maze of leafless '''twigs''' and dusky spires cut sharp against the soft blueness of the evening sky.}}
# {{lb|en|bodybuilding|slang}} Somebody, or one of their [[body part]]s, not looking [[developed]].
#* {{quote-web|en|archivedate=2024-02-16|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240216141736/https://www.bodybuilding.com/fun/weik39.htm|url=https://www.bodybuilding.com/fun/weik39.htm|title=Successful Tips and Tricks For Contest Prep!|work=Bodybuilding.com|author=Matt Weik, CSCS|date=2007-02-24|passage=You need to find a source of motivation and play off of that. Whether it be the jock in high school that always called you fat, or the guy who picked on you and called you a '''twig'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|work=Showbiz CheatSheet|date=2022-07-19|title=Arnold Schwarzenegger’s Most Dangerous Mistake on ‘True Lies’: ‘It Would Have Put Us Back 30 Days in the Production’|author=Jason Rossi|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/arnold-schwarzenegger-dangerous-mistake-true-lies.html/|passage=Schwarzenegger was long past his professional bodybuilding days when he and Carrere shot the tango scene, but he wasn’t a '''twig'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240216141739/https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/arnold-schwarzenegger-dangerous-mistake-true-lies.html/|archivedate=16 February 2024}}

