#* {{quote-book|en|year=1930 |tlr=w:en:Marmaduke Pickthall |title=w:en:The Meaning of the Glorious Koran|section=surah 28, verse 29 |pageurl=https://archive.org/details/meaningofgloriou0000unse_l1d9/page/397/mode/2up |page=397 |location=New York |publisher=Alfred A Knop|text=Then, when Moses had fulfilled the term, and was '''travelling''' with his housefolk, he saw in the distance a fire and said unto his housefolk: Bide ye (here). Lo! I see in the distance a fire; peradventure I shall bring you tidings thence, or a brand from the fire that ye may warm yourselves.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=2012-06-09
|author=Owen Phillips
|title=Euro 2012: Netherlands 0-1 Denmark
|work=w:BBC Sport
|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/18138777
|page=
|passage=And Netherlands, backed by a typically noisy and colourful '''travelling''' support, started the second period in blistering fashion and could have had four goals within 10 minutes|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220215144453/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/18138777}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Snejana Farberov|title=Dad shot dead in road-rage attack after splashing windshield fluid on BMW|magazine=w:New York Post|url=https://nypost.com/2022/07/21/dad-shot-dead-after-splashing-windshield-fluid-on-bmw/|date=2022-07-21|passage=Dennis Anderson, 45, and Brandy Goldsbury, 46, were '''traveling''' from the beach in Lincoln City on the Oregon coast back to their home in Tigard around 8:30 p.m. July 13 when they spotted a black BMW 3 Series trying to pass them, according to reporting in The Oregonian.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816233207/https://nypost.com/2022/07/21/dad-shot-dead-after-splashing-windshield-fluid-on-bmw/}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[pass]] from one place to another; to move or [[transmit]].
#: {{syn|en|range<qq:ballistics>}}
#: {{ux|en|Soundwaves can '''travel''' through water.}}
#: {{ux|en|The supposedly secret news of Mary's engagement '''travelled''' quickly through her group of friends.}}
